<title>GERMANY: Bonn sees German 1996 grain crop up 3 pct.</title>
<headline>Bonn sees German 1996 grain crop up 3 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1996-08-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Germany's 1996 grain crop was estimated at 41 million tonnes compared with 39.9 million tonnes, the Bonn farm ministry said on Thursday.</p>
<p>The ministry also said the average yield would be 6.1 tonnes per hectare, unchanged from last year.</p>
<p>The ministry stressed the figure was preliminary because harvesting was delayed. Only two-thirds of grain had been cut in the west, while in the east, only 30 to 50 percent had been harvested. --Bonn newsroom, 49 228 26097150</p>
</text>
